IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 111 and 115 (piece dg1): the Court of Chancery's
-- jurisdiction over corporate instruments and provisions of this title, and forum selection provisions.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view. (Section 115(b) defines "internal corporate claims",
-- which sections 102(f) and 109(b) use; they call the rule here.)
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- The Court of Chancery is an official: no seat. What it may hear is encoded as what it means for the person who
-- sues or is sued.

§ `Section 111 -- Jurisdiction to interpret, apply, enforce or determine the validity of corporate instruments and provisions of this title`

-- src:161 | (a) Any civil action to interpret, apply, enforce or determine the validity of the provisions of:
-- src:162 | (1) The certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of a corporation;
-- src:163 | (2) Any instrument, document or agreement (i) by which a corporation creates or sells, or offers to create or sell, any of its stock, or any rights or options respecting its stock, or (ii) to which a corporation and 1 or more holders of its stock are parties, and pursuant to which any such holder or holders sell or offer …
-- src:164 | (3) Any written restrictions on the transfer, registration of transfer or ownership of securities under § 202 of this title;
-- src:165 | (4) Any proxy under § 212 or § 215 of this title;
-- src:166 | (5) Any voting trust or other voting agreement under § 218 of this title;
-- src:167 | (6) Any agreement, certificate of merger or consolidation, or certificate of ownership and merger governed by §§ 251-253, §§ 255-258, §§ 263-264, or § 267 of this title;
-- src:168 | (7) Any certificate of conversion under § 265 or § 266 of this title;
-- src:169 | (8) Any certificate of domestication, transfer or continuance under § 388, § 389 or § 390 of this title; or
-- src:170 | (9) Any other instrument, document, agreement, or certificate required by any provision of this title;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 111(a) (src:161-170)
DECLARE `s 111(a) Subject of the action` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of a corporation`
    `an instrument, document or agreement by which a corporation creates or sells, or offers to create or sell, any of its stock, or any rights or options respecting its stock`
    `an instrument, document or agreement to which a corporation and 1 or more holders of its stock are parties, and pursuant to which any such holder sells or offers to sell any of such stock`
    `an instrument, document or agreement by which a corporation agrees to sell, lease or exchange any of its property or assets, and which by its terms provides that 1 or more holders of its stock approve of or consent to the sale, lease or exchange`
    `written restrictions on the transfer, registration of transfer or ownership of securities under § 202`
    `a proxy under § 212 or § 215`
    `a voting trust or other voting agreement under § 218`
    `an agreement, certificate of merger or consolidation, or certificate of ownership and merger governed by §§ 251-253, §§ 255-258, §§ 263-264, or § 267`
    `a certificate of conversion under § 265 or § 266`
    `a certificate of domestication, transfer or continuance under § 388, § 389 or § 390`
    `any other instrument, document, agreement or certificate required by any provision of this title`
    `a matter that is none of those`

-- Any civil action to interpret, apply, enforce or determine the validity of the provisions of the subjects
-- listed may be brought in the Court of Chancery, except to the extent that a statute confers exclusive
-- jurisdiction on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery. A matter that is none of the
-- listed subjects is not covered by subsection (a) (NOTHING).
-- src:161 | (a) Any civil action to interpret, apply, enforce or determine the validity of the provisions of:
-- src:171 | may be brought in the Court of Chancery, except to the extent that a statute confers exclusive jurisdiction on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 111(a) (src:161) (src:171)
GIVEN subject IS A `s 111(a) Subject of the action`
      `a statute confers exclusive jurisdiction on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(a) the civil action may be brought in the Court of Chancery` subject `a statute confers exclusive jurisdiction on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `a matter that is none of those` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (NOT (`a statute confers exclusive jurisdiction on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery`))

-- Subsection (b): any civil action to interpret, apply or enforce any provision of this title may be brought in
-- the Court of Chancery. (It does not say "determine the validity", and it has no exception for exclusive
-- jurisdiction elsewhere.)
-- src:172 | (b) Any civil action to interpret, apply or enforce any provision of this title may be brought in the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 111(b) (src:172)
GIVEN `the civil action is to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(b) the civil action may be brought in the Court of Chancery` `the civil action is to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of this title` MEANS
    IF `the civil action is to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of this title`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 115 -- Forum selection provisions`

-- Subsection (b): "internal corporate claims" are claims, including claims in the right of the corporation,
-- (i) based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director, officer or stockholder in such capacity,
-- or (ii) as to which this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery. Whether the title "confers
-- jurisdiction" through sections 111(a) and (b) is a fork (see the Fork register): the rule below takes the
-- jurisdiction as a fact, and `s 115(b)(ii) ...` derives it from section 111.
-- src:217 | (b) “Internal corporate claims” means claims, including claims in the right of the corporation, (i) that are based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity, or (ii) as to which this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 115(b) (src:217)
GIVEN `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(b) the claim is an internal corporate claim` `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` MEANS
        `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity`
     OR `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim`

-- src:217 | (b) “Internal corporate claims” means claims, including claims in the right of the corporation, (i) that are based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity, or (ii) as to which this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 115(b) (src:217)
GIVEN `section 111 says the claim may be brought in the Court of Chancery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `another section of this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(b)(ii) this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` `section 111 says the claim may be brought in the Court of Chancery` `another section of this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 111 says the claim may be brought in the Court of Chancery`
    WHEN JUST permitted THEN permitted OR `another section of this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `another section of this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim`

-- Subsection (a): the certificate or bylaws may require, consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements,
-- that any or all internal corporate claims be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this
-- State; and no provision may prohibit bringing such claims in the courts of this State. A provision that does
-- neither is not addressed by subsection (a) (NOTHING).
-- src:216 | (a) The certificate of incorporation or the bylaws may require, consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements, that any or all internal corporate claims shall be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this State, and no provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws may prohibit bringing such claims in the courts of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 115(a) (src:216)
GIVEN `the provision requires that internal corporate claims be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision prohibits bringing internal corporate claims in the courts of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(a) the provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws is permitted` `the provision requires that internal corporate claims be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this State` `the provision prohibits bringing internal corporate claims in the courts of this State` `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements` MEANS
    IF `the provision prohibits bringing internal corporate claims in the courts of this State`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the provision requires that internal corporate claims be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this State`
         THEN JUST `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (c): for claims that are not internal corporate claims, the certificate or bylaws may require
-- stockholders, acting as stockholders or in the right of the corporation, to bring them only in prescribed
-- forums, if the claims relate to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or
-- powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers; provided that the requirement is
-- consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements and allows a stockholder to bring the claims in at least
-- 1 court in this State that has jurisdiction over them. For an internal corporate claim subsection (c) does not
-- speak (NOTHING).
-- src:218 | (c) With respect to claims that are not internal corporate claims, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws may require stockholders, when acting in their capacity as stockholders or in the right of the corporation, to bring any or all such claims only in 1 or more prescribed forums or venues, if such claims relate to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers; provided that such requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements and allows a stockholder to bring such claims in at least 1 court in this State that has jurisdiction over such claims.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 115(c) (src:218)
GIVEN `the claim is an internal corporate claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder is acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement allows the stockholder to bring the claim in at least 1 court in this State that has jurisdiction over the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(c) the certificate or the bylaws may require the stockholder to bring the claim only in the prescribed forums` `the claim is an internal corporate claim` `the stockholder is acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation` `the claim relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers` `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements` `the requirement allows the stockholder to bring the claim in at least 1 court in this State that has jurisdiction over the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim is an internal corporate claim`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the stockholder is acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation`
               AND `the claim relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers`
               AND `the requirement is consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements`
               AND `the requirement allows the stockholder to bring the claim in at least 1 court in this State that has jurisdiction over the claim`)
